    "title": "Who Owns My Infrastructure?",
    "url": "http://RepGaydos.com/infrastructureown",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Who Owns My Infrastructure?\nWith the number of roads and bridges having been affected by the recent flooding and landslides, we frequently get asked who has the responsibility for fixing things. Now you can see, \"Who Owns My Infrastructure?\" an interactive map which allows you to search by address to see what roadways in Allegheny County are state, county, municipal or private.\nView the map here.\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "A Pennsylvania legislator is promoting an existing interactive online map that allows residents to look up who is responsible for roads and bridges in Allegheny County by searching their address. The map categorizes infrastructure as state, county, municipal, or privately owned. This appears to be a informational resource shared in response to flooding and landslide damage in the area.",
      "action_type": "statement",
      "topics": [
        "infrastructure"
      ],
      "spin_flag": false
    }
