    "raw_text": "Gaydos to Participate in Union Pacific  Big Boy No. 4014 Whistle Stop in Leetsdale\nJuly 10, 2026\nWHAT:\nRep. Valerie Gaydos (R-Allegheny), a commissioner on the Pennsylvania Commission for the United States Semiquincentennial (America250PA), will participate in Leetsdale Borough's celebration of the historic visit of Union Pacific’s Big Boy No. 4014. During the event, Gaydos will present a Pennsylvania House of Representatives citation recognizing the borough for hosting a Big Boy No. 4014 whistle stop.\nWHO:\nGaydos (R-Allegheny); Leetsdale Borough Mayor Sandra Ford; Leetsdale Borough Council President Maria Napolitano; and Leetsdale Borough Fire Chief Wes James.\nWHEN:\nSaturday, July 11, program from 5:30-6 p.m.\nAnticipated arrival of Union Pacific Big Boy No. 4014 at 6:15 p.m.\nWHERE:\nHenle Park,\n373 Beaver St., Leetsdale\n.\nThe viewing location will be at Ferry Street Railroad Crossing near the Subway\n.\nMEDIA PARKING:\nReserved media parking is available next to the Subway sandwich shop at Ferry Street and Ohio River Boulevard. Media must contact the Leetsdale Borough Office at 724-266-4820 in advance to be placed on the media parking list and reserve a parking space.\nNOTE:\nTrain arrival and departure times are subject to change. The anticipated departure of Union Pacific Big Boy No. 4014 is 6:45 p.m.\nPlease see the attached information, courtesy of Leetsdale Borough.\nMedia contact: Rick Leiner, 717-260-6437,\nrleiner@pahousegop.com\n.\nRepresentative Valerie Gaydos\n44th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Rick Leiner\n717.260.6437\nrleiner@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
